course: dictionary
lesson: 10151
title: Many meanings of throw
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Throw is a small word with many meanings. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right. «Throw the ball to me.» Here throw means to send something through the air with your arm.
explain: «She threw her coat on the bed.» Here throw means to put something somewhere quickly or carelessly. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «she sent her coat through the air on the bed» make sense? No, so this is the other meaning.
explain: Throw can also mean to confuse someone. «The question threw me» does not mean the question flew through the air. It means I could not understand it. Always ask: what would fit here?
fact: «Throw» means to send something through the air with your arm.
fact: «Throw» can also mean to put something somewhere quickly or carelessly.
fact: «Throw» can mean to confuse someone, as in «The question threw me».
fact: The forms are throw, throws, threw, thrown and throwing. Use threw for yesterday, and thrown after has or have.
fact: «A good throw» is a noun: an act of throwing, or a turn at throwing.
exercise: «Throw the ball to me.» What does throw mean here? | To move your body suddenly | To put something down carelessly | * To send something through the air with your arm | To confuse someone
exercise: «The question threw me.» What does threw mean here? | * To confuse | To send through the air | To move quickly | To put something away
exercise: In «a good throw», what kind of word is throw? | * A noun | A verb | A full stop | An adjective
test: «She threw her coat on the bed.» What does threw mean here? | * To put something somewhere quickly or carelessly | To put something somewhere quickly or carelessly | To confuse | To send through the air
test: Yesterday Sam ___ the ball to the goalkeeper. Which word fits? | thrown | throwed | * threw | threw
exam: «You never kick or throw a ball at someone who is not ready.» Why not? | Because the ball gets too wet | Because it makes a good noise | Because throw means to catch | * Because it hurts and starts fights
